      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "SettingUpAComputerObserve",
          "kind": "step",
          "title": "Observe",
          "description": "Observe the parts of a computer system, what each one does, and how they connect.",
          "imageName": null,
          "autoplayVO": true,
          "voClip": "ICT_Setup_Observe",
          "captions": [
            {
              "text": "A computer system is made of parts that work together. Some parts take data in, some process it, and some give information out.",
              "duration": 11.324
            },
            {
              "text": "The monitor is an output device. It shows us text, pictures, and video.",
              "duration": 8.804
            },
            {
              "text": "The keyboard and the mouse are input devices. We use them to type, to point, and to click.",
              "duration": 9.428
            },
            {
              "text": "The system unit holds the parts that process and store data. Let's lift off its cover and look inside.",
              "duration": 9.692
            },
            {
              "text": "The large circuit board is the motherboard. Every part connects to it, so the parts can share power and data.",
              "duration": 9.836
            },
            {
              "text": "This is the central processing unit, or CPU. It carries out instructions and does calculations. It is the brain of the computer.",
              "duration": 12.764
            },
            {
              "text": "These are the memory modules, called RAM. RAM holds the programs and data you are using right now. When the power goes off, RAM is emptied.",
              "duration": 13.652
            },
            {
              "text": "The storage drive keeps your files and programs, even when the computer is switched off.",
              "duration": 7.82
            },
            {
              "text": "The power supply unit changes electricity from the wall socket into the power that the parts need.",
              "duration": 8.084
            },
            {
              "text": "Now let's turn the system unit around. At the back are the ports, where the cables connect.",
              "duration": 8.78
            },
            {
              "text": "Each kind of cable has its own shape of port. A plug only fits the port that matches it, and only one way round.",
              "duration": 10.7
            },
            {
              "text": "The monitor cable goes into the HDMI port. The keyboard and mouse go into USB ports. The network cable goes into the LAN port.",
              "duration": 13.124
            },
            {
              "text": "Connect every cable first, and switch on the power last. Before you open a computer, always switch it off and unplug it.",
              "duration": 11.156
            },
            {
              "text": "Select Next to continue.",
              "duration": -1
            }
          ],
          "buttons": [
            {
              "id": "observe_replay",
              "text": "Replay",
